_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105878.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #105875, Fixes #112647\r\n\r\nCurrently, numeric inspector properties support `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` implicitly (and are used by many editor classes), but the `@export_range` does not recognize this. This PR allows `@export_range` annotation to use the following types:\r\nVector2, Vector2I, Rect2, Rect2I, Vector3, Vector3I, Vector4, Vector4I, Transform2D, Transform3D, Plane, Quaternion, AABB, Basis, and Projection\r\n\r\nIt does this by replacing the float and int type check done in master with a custom check that was already partially implemented.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105878/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":12,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105878/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}